{"title":"Equate","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>We <b>equate</b> two quantities when we set them equal in an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a>.  This technique, besides being the fundamental ingredient for much of modern <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a>, is particularly useful when solving <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Word_problem\" title=\"Word problem\">word problems</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equate&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\"> 2006 AIME I Problem 5</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equate&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">Equation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Category_theory\" title=\"Category theory\">Category theory</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Equate&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201350\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 16/1000000\nPost‐expand include size